\section{Hit-rate observability}{

Cache counters are session-local diagnostics for the read path. A successful
cache read increments \code{hit}; a missing entry, a disabled namespace, an entry
without a fingerprint sidecar, an unreadable \code{.rds} file, a malformed
sidecar, or a digest mismatch increments \code{miss}, because the caller then has
to recompute the artifact. \code{hit_rate} is \code{hit / (hit + miss)} and is \code{NaN}
before a namespace has had any reads. Counters start at package load and are
reset for a namespace when \code{\link[=cacs_clear_cache]{cacs_clear_cache()}} removes its files. If a
repeat workflow is still slow, inspect \code{cacs_get_cache_state()$counters[[1]]}:
zero hits in a namespace usually means the second run is not reading the
cache entries you expect.
}

